# Form Patterns

All interactive forms use **react-hook-form** + **zod** + **shadcn/ui Form** primitives.

## Stack

```bash
pnpm add react-hook-form zod@3 @hookform/resolvers
pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add form checkbox   # add other inputs as needed
```

Use **zod v3** — `@hookform/resolvers` does not yet support zod v4.

## File layout

| Location | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `lib/*-schema.ts` | Zod schema, inferred type, default values |
| `components/ui/form.tsx` | shadcn `Form`, `FormField`, `FormItem`, etc. |
| `components/ui/form-text-field.tsx` | Reusable labeled text/email/tel input |
| `components/ui/form-textarea-field.tsx` | Reusable labeled textarea |
| `lib/form-field-styles.ts` | Shared `on-primary` label/input classes |
| `app/<feature>/…` | Feature-specific field groups and form shell |

Split field groups into separate components when a form exceeds ~100 lines.

## Schema conventions

- Define schema with `z.object({ … })` in `lib/`
- Export `type FormValues = z.infer<typeof schema>`
- Export matching `defaultValues` object
- Wire with `useForm({ resolver: zodResolver(schema), defaultValues })`

## UI conventions

- Wrap with `<Form {...form}>` and native `<form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>`
- Use `FormField` + `FormItem` + `FormLabel` + `FormControl` + `FormMessage`
- Prefer `FormTextField` / `FormTextareaField` for standard inputs
- Style fields with `formFieldLabelClass`, `formFieldInputClass` from `lib/form-field-styles.ts`
- Match existing `on-primary` filter/search styling on blue content pages
- Submit buttons use `Button` with `variant='inverse'` and `size='xl'` on content pages
- Add `"use client"` only on form components; keep `page.tsx` as a Server Component shell

## Do not

- Build custom validation or uncontrolled form state outside react-hook-form
- Duplicate shadcn form primitives — extend `components/ui/form-*` instead
- Hardcode field lists that already exist in `lib/` data sources
